hi Darwin,
 The definition of 'site' in this model and related models (N-mixture model, occupancy model , etc..) is essentially 'independent unit'   -- so whether it is a grid of traps or individual traps is less important than what is reasonably be understood as an independent population exposed to sampling.   So for example if you have a grid of 100 traps with 100 m spacing  and you are interested in a squirrel or small rodent then camera trap locations are probably reasonable 'sites'. But if you're sampling mountain lions than not so much.   You need to think about that and then make the call because I'm afraid there aren't really rules-of-thumb on the matter.

regards
andy

